WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.230
A student starts a sentence:

2
00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:03.540
«En arrivant à la gare»,

3
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.570
on arriving at the station.

4
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.380
Then the sentence goes wrong,

5
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.660
and a French reader sees
the train itself arriving.

6
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.580
Oops. Yet the ending A,

7
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.810
N, T is real French:

8
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.620
«Elles sont sorties en
courant.» They ran out.

9
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:21.140
So English swimming, smoking, leaving,

10
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.470
working: can they all
take those three letters?

11
00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.260
In this mission, you'll run verbs
through a participle factory:

12
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.410
cut, stick, done.

13
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.970
Then you'll put two actions on a timeline.

14
00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.780
Which one finished first?

15
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.460
Your mission: work out when an English I,

16
00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.760
N, G ending can become French A,

17
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.640
N, T, and when it can't.
